data:{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":"02c87599-a5b7-449e-b878-6ea70536dd38","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"result\":{\"ok\":true,\"data\":{\"type\":\"evidence_pack\",\"skill_id\":\"us_equity_upcoming_event_calendar\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-25T15:41:40Z\",\"data\":{\"status\":\"ok\",\"as_of\":\"2026-09-25T15:41:40.044494Z\",\"asset\":{\"asset_type\":\"us_equity\",\"symbol\":\"NVDA\",\"name\":\"NVIDIA Corporation\",\"exchange\":\"NASDAQ\",\"sector\":\"Technology\",\"industry\":\"Semiconductors\"},\"window\":{\"start\":\"2026-09-25T15:41:40.044494Z\",\"end\":\"2026-10-02T15:41:40.044494Z\",\"timezone\":\"UTC\"},\"report\":\"1. Core PCE Price Index MoM (Aug) / Core PCE Price Index YoY (Aug) / PCE Price Index MoM (Aug) / PCE Price Index YoY (Aug) release is scheduled for September 30, 2026 as a U.S. macro event. It is important to NVIDIA because inflation data influences monetary policy expectations and equity discount rates.\\n2. NVIDIA Dividend schedule is confirmed for payment on October 1, 2026 as a company event. It is important to NVIDIA shareholders as a scheduled cash distribution.\\n3. ISM Manufacturing PMI (Sep) release is scheduled for October 1, 2026 as a U.S. macro event. It is important to NVIDIA because manufacturing demand data informs expectations for semiconductor industry conditions.\\n4. Non Farm Payrolls (Sep) / Nonfarm Payrolls Private (Sep) release is scheduled for October 2, 2026 as a U.S. macro event. It is important to NVIDIA because employment data signals broader economic demand trends relevant to tech sector revenue.\\n5. U-6 Unemployment Rate (Sep) / Unemployment Rate (Sep) release is scheduled for October 2, 2026 as a U.S. macro event. It is important to NVIDIA because labor market health signals consumer and business spending trends that impact technology demand.\",\"events\":[{\"event_id\":\"event_a0535dd6ce90beb6d3037bf3\",\"identity_version\":\"v1\",\"identity_strength\":\"conditional\",\"dedupe_policy\":\"facts_match\",\"scope\"